<section class="bg-cream py-10 lg:py-12"><div class="container-x">
  <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_270px]">
    <article class="card prose p-6 sm:p-8">
<h2 class="mod-h2">Important Educational Thinkers</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Dewey, Vygotsky and Skinner</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">UGC NET/JRF &amp; Assistant Professor Paper-1 — December 2026</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Master Association</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">John Dewey → Pragmatism → Learning by Doing → Reflective Thinking</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Lev Vygotsky → Social Constructivism → ZPD → Scaffolding</p>
<p class="mod-strong">B. F. Skinner → Behaviourism → Operant Conditioning → Reinforcement</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">Part I: John Dewey</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Learning by Doing and Reflective Thinking</h3>
<h2 class="mod-h2">1. Introduction</h2>
<p>John Dewey (1859–1952) American philosopher, psychologist और educational thinker थे।</p>
<p>Education में उन्हें मुख्यतः निम्न concepts से associate करें:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Pragmatism</li><li>Instrumentalism</li><li>Progressive Education</li><li>Learning by Doing</li><li>Experience-based Learning</li><li>Problem-solving</li><li>Reflective Thinking</li><li>Democratic Education</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Exam Association</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Dewey → Pragmatism → Experience → Activity → Problem-Solving → Reflection</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">2. Dewey’s Concept of Education</h2>
<p>Dewey के अनुसार education केवल future life की preparation नहीं है। Education स्वयं जीवन और continuous growth की process है।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Education is a continuous reconstruction of experience.</p>
<p>Learner नई experiences को previous experiences से जोड़ता है, उन पर reflection करता है और future action के लिए meaning विकसित करता है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Core Formula</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Dewey = Experience + Inquiry + Reflection + Action</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">3. Learning by Doing</h2>
<p>Learning by Doing का अर्थ है कि learner meaningful activities में actively participate करके सीखता है।</p>
<p>इसमें learner:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Observe करता है।</li><li>Questions पूछता है।</li><li>Experiment करता है।</li><li>Problem solve करता है।</li><li>Results देखता है।</li><li>अपनी experience पर reflection करता है।</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Example</h3>
<p>Teacher students को “Environmental Pollution” की definition याद कराने के बजाय campus waste का survey कराता है।</p>
<p>Learners:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Waste sources identify करते हैं।</li><li>Data collect करते हैं।</li><li>Causes analyse करते हैं।</li><li>Solutions propose करते हैं।</li><li>अपने project पर reflection करते हैं।</li></ul>
<p>यह Dewey के Learning by Doing का example है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">4. Experience and Education</h2>
<p>Dewey के अनुसार प्रत्येक activity educational नहीं होती।</p>
<p>Good educational experience में दो principles महत्त्वपूर्ण हैं:</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">4.1 Continuity of Experience</h3>
<p>Present experience future learning और development को प्रभावित करती है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Present Experience → Future Learning</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">4.2 Interaction</h3>
<p>Learning learner की internal conditions और external environment के interaction से होती है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Learning = Learner × Environment</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Exam Trap</h3>
<p>केवल physical activity करवाना Learning by Doing नहीं है। Activity:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Purposeful</li><li>Meaningful</li><li>Connected with objectives</li><li>Followed by reflection</li></ul>
<p>होनी चाहिए।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">5. Reflective Thinking</h2>
<p>Reflective Thinking किसी belief या proposed knowledge को evidence और consequences के आधार पर carefully examine करना है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Dewey’s Reflective Process</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Problem → Observation/Data → Hypothesis → Reasoning → Testing → Conclusion</p>
<p class="mod-tag">1. Felt Difficulty</p>
<p>Learner को problem या doubt महसूस होता है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">2. Problem Identification</p>
<p>Problem को clearly define किया जाता है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">3. Hypothesis</p>
<p>Possible solutions develop किए जाते हैं।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">4. Reasoning</p>
<p>Solutions के implications analyse किए जाते हैं।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">5. Testing</p>
<p>Evidence और experience से hypothesis test की जाती है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">6. Conclusion</p>
<p>Most appropriate solution स्वीकार किया जाता है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">6. Dewey’s Democratic Education</h2>
<p>Dewey classroom और school को democratic society का miniature form मानते थे।</p>
<p>Democratic classroom में:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Participation</li><li>Cooperation</li><li>Discussion</li><li>Shared responsibility</li><li>Respect for different views</li><li>Problem-solving</li></ul>
<p>को encourage किया जाता है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Teacher’s Role</h3>
<p>Teacher:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Learning experiences design करता है।</li><li>Problems प्रस्तुत करता है।</li><li>Inquiry facilitate करता है।</li><li>Resources उपलब्ध कराता है।</li><li>Ready-made answers impose नहीं करता।</li><li>Reflection encourage करता है।</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Learner’s Role</h3>
<p>Learner:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Active participant</li><li>Investigator</li><li>Problem-solver</li><li>Collaborator</li><li>Reflective thinker</li></ul>
<p>होता है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">7. Classroom Applications of Dewey</h2>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Project Method</li><li>Problem-solving</li><li>Laboratory activity</li><li>Field visit</li><li>Case study</li><li>Group investigation</li><li>Community survey</li><li>Experiential learning</li><li>Reflective journal</li><li>Democratic discussion</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Thinker Connection</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Dewey → Philosophical Foundation of Project-Based Learning</p>
<p class="mod-tag">William H. Kilpatrick → Project Method</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">8. Exam Traps: Dewey</h2>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Dewey को Idealism से associate न करें; वे Pragmatism से संबंधित हैं।</li><li>Learning by Doing केवल mechanical activity नहीं है।</li><li>Experience के साथ reflection आवश्यक है।</li><li>Dewey teacher को completely remove नहीं करते; teacher experience designer और facilitator है।</li><li>Dewey competition की तुलना में cooperation और democracy पर अधिक emphasis देते हैं।</li><li>Project Method का direct association Kilpatrick से है, जबकि philosophical foundation Dewey से जुड़ा है।</li></ul>
<h2 class="mod-h2">Part II: Lev Vygotsky</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">ZPD, Social Constructivism and Scaffolding</h3>
<h2 class="mod-h2">9. Introduction</h2>
<p>Lev Vygotsky (1896–1934) Russian psychologist थे।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Main Associations</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Vygotsky → Social Constructivism → Social Interaction → Language → ZPD → Scaffolding</p>
<p>Vygotsky के अनुसार learning केवल individual mental activity नहीं है। Knowledge social और cultural interaction के माध्यम से construct होती है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Core Formula</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Learning = Social Interaction + Language + Cultural Tools + Guided Participation</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">10. Social Constructivism</h2>
<p>Social Constructivism के अनुसार learner knowledge को:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Teacher</li><li>Peers</li><li>Parents</li><li>Experts</li><li>Culture</li><li>Language</li></ul>
<p>के interaction से construct करता है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Important Principle</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Learning first occurs at the social level and later becomes internalised at the individual level.</p>
<p>पहले learner किसी task को guidance के साथ करता है; धीरे-धीरे वह उसे independently perform करने लगता है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">11. Zone of Proximal Development</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">निकटस्थ विकास क्षेत्र</h3>
<p>ZPD उस difference को दर्शाता है जो learner:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Independently कर सकता है</li><li>Guidance के साथ कर सकता है</li></ul>
<p>के बीच होता है।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">ZPD = Potential Performance with Guidance − Independent Performance</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Three Learning Zones</h3>
<p class="mod-tag">1. What Learner Can Do Independently</p>
<p>Task learner के actual development level में है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">2. What Learner Can Do with Support</p>
<p>यही Zone of Proximal Development है।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">3. What Learner Cannot Yet Do Even with Support</p>
<p>Task learner के current developmental reach से बाहर है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">12. ZPD Example</h2>
<p>एक learner simple percentage independently calculate कर सकता है, लेकिन weighted average नहीं।</p>
<p>Teacher:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Formula का hint देता है।</li><li>Solved example दिखाता है।</li><li>Steps explain करता है।</li><li>Guided practice कराता है।</li></ul>
<p>Learner assistance के साथ SGPA calculate कर लेता है।</p>
<p>यह task learner की ZPD में है।</p>
<p>कुछ practice के बाद learner independently SGPA calculate करता है। इसका अर्थ है कि assisted performance internalised हो गई।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">13. More Knowledgeable Other</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">अधिक जानकार व्यक्ति</h3>
<p>More Knowledgeable Other—MKO वह व्यक्ति या source है जिसके पास learner से अधिक knowledge या competence होती है।</p>
<p>MKO हो सकता है:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Teacher</li><li>Parent</li><li>Skilled peer</li><li>Expert</li><li>Mentor</li><li>Digital tutor</li><li>Learning resource</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Exam Trap</h3>
<p>MKO हमेशा teacher नहीं होता। Competent peer भी MKO हो सकता है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">14. Scaffolding</h2>
<p>Scaffolding learner को task complete करने के लिए temporary, structured support देना है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Examples</h3>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Hints</li><li>Prompts</li><li>Guided questions</li><li>Worked examples</li><li>Partial solution</li><li>Visual cues</li><li>Peer assistance</li><li>Feedback</li><li>Task simplification</li></ul>
<p>Learner competence बढ़ने पर support धीरे-धीरे हटाया जाता है।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Scaffolding = Temporary Support + Gradual Withdrawal</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Scaffolding Process</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Model → Guide → Practise Together → Reduce Support → Independent Performance</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">15. Historical Exam Point</h2>
<p>Scaffolding concept Vygotsky’s ZPD से strongly related है, लेकिन scaffolding term Wood, Bruner और Ross से associated है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Exam Trap</h3>
<p>यदि प्रश्न हो:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>ZPD किसने दिया? → Vygotsky</li><li>Scaffolding term किनसे जुड़ा है? → Wood, Bruner and Ross</li><li>Scaffolding का theoretical आधार? → Vygotsky’s ZPD</li></ul>
<h2 class="mod-h2">16. Language and Thought</h2>
<p>Vygotsky ने cognitive development में language को central role दिया।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Social Speech</h3>
<p>दूसरों के साथ communication के लिए।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Private Speech</h3>
<p>Learner स्वयं से बोलकर behaviour और problem-solving guide करता है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>Child कहता है:</p>
<p>“पहले यह step करना है, फिर next number जोड़ना है।”</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Inner Speech</h3>
<p>Private speech धीरे-धीरे silent internal thinking में बदल जाती है।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Social Speech → Private Speech → Inner Speech</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">17. Classroom Applications of Vygotsky</h2>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Cooperative learning</li><li>Peer tutoring</li><li>Collaborative problem-solving</li><li>Guided practice</li><li>Reciprocal teaching</li><li>Think–Pair–Share</li><li>Teacher questioning</li><li>Group project</li><li>Dialogic teaching</li><li>Gradual release of responsibility</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Teacher’s Role</h3>
<p>Teacher:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Learner का actual level assess करता है।</li><li>ZPD के भीतर task देता है।</li><li>Appropriate support देता है।</li><li>Interaction organise करता है।</li><li>Support धीरे-धीरे withdraw करता है।</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Learner’s Role</h3>
<p>Learner:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Interaction करता है।</li><li>Help seek करता है।</li><li>Peer के साथ collaborate करता है।</li><li>Language द्वारा thinking organise करता है।</li><li>Gradually independent बनता है।</li></ul>
<h2 class="mod-h2">18. Piaget vs Vygotsky</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Recall Formula</h3>
<p class="mod-tag">Piaget = Individual Construction</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Vygotsky = Social Construction</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">19. Exam Traps: Vygotsky</h2>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>ZPD independent performance नहीं, assisted potential का zone है।</li><li>बहुत आसान task ZPD में नहीं होगा।</li><li>Impossible task भी ZPD में नहीं होगा।</li><li>Scaffolding permanent support नहीं है।</li><li>MKO केवल teacher नहीं होता।</li><li>Private speech immaturity नहीं, self-regulation का tool हो सकती है।</li><li>Vygotsky social और cultural context पर emphasis देते हैं।</li></ul>
<h2 class="mod-h2">Part III: B. F. Skinner</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Operant Conditioning, Reinforcement and Programmed Instruction</h3>
<h2 class="mod-h2">20. Introduction</h2>
<p>Burrhus Frederic Skinner (1904–1990) American behaviourist psychologist थे।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Main Associations</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Skinner → Behaviourism → Operant Conditioning → Reinforcement → Programmed Instruction</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Core Formula</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Behaviour → Consequence → Future Behaviour</p>
<p>Skinner के अनुसार behaviour उसके consequences से strengthen या weaken हो सकता है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">21. Operant Conditioning</h2>
<p>Operant behaviour वह behaviour है जो learner environment पर operate करते हुए प्रदर्शित करता है और जिसके consequences future behaviour को प्रभावित करते हैं।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>Student नियमित assignment submit करता है। Teacher timely praise और feedback देता है। Assignment submission बढ़ जाता है।</p>
<p>यह reinforcement का example है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">22. Reinforcement</h2>
<p>Reinforcement का उद्देश्य behaviour की frequency बढ़ाना है।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Reinforcement always aims to increase behaviour.</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">22.1 Positive Reinforcement</h3>
<p>Desirable behaviour के बाद pleasant stimulus add करना।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Formula</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Positive Reinforcement = Add Pleasant Stimulus → Behaviour Increases</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Examples</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Correct answer पर praise</li><li>Good performance पर certificate</li><li>Assignment completion पर extra choice</li><li>Participation पर recognition</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">22.2 Negative Reinforcement</h3>
<p>Desirable behaviour के बाद unpleasant condition remove करना।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Formula</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Negative Reinforcement = Remove Unpleasant Condition → Behaviour Increases</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>Students निर्धारित work समय पर complete करते हैं, इसलिए teacher additional remedial drill हटा देता है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Exam Trap</h3>
<p>Negative reinforcement punishment नहीं है।</p>
<p>“Negative” का अर्थ stimulus हटाना है; इसका अर्थ undesirable या harmful नहीं।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">23. Punishment</h2>
<p>Punishment का उद्देश्य undesirable behaviour की frequency कम करना है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Punishment aims to decrease behaviour.</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">23.1 Positive Punishment</h3>
<p>Behaviour कम करने के लिए unpleasant consequence add करना।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>Repeated disruption पर formal warning देना।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">23.2 Negative Punishment</h3>
<p>Behaviour कम करने के लिए pleasant privilege remove करना।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>Misuse के कारण activity privilege temporarily हटाना।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Important Ethical Point</h3>
<p>Educational punishment:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Humiliating</li><li>Physically harmful</li><li>Discriminatory</li><li>Excessive</li></ul>
<p>नहीं होना चाहिए।</p>
<p>Positive discipline, feedback और restorative approaches generally अधिक appropriate हैं।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">24. Reinforcement vs Punishment</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Master Rule</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Reinforcement increases behaviour.
Punishment decreases behaviour.
Positive adds; Negative removes.</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">25. Types of Reinforcers</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Primary Reinforcer</h3>
<p>Biological needs से related:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Food</li><li>Rest</li><li>Comfort</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Secondary/Conditioned Reinforcer</h3>
<p>Learned value:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Marks</li><li>Praise</li><li>Certificate</li><li>Token</li><li>Grade</li><li>Recognition</li></ul>
<h2 class="mod-h2">26. Reinforcement Schedules</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">26.1 Continuous Reinforcement</h3>
<p>Every correct response reinforce किया जाता है।</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>New behaviour establish करने में useful</li><li>Extinction relatively जल्दी हो सकती है</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">26.2 Fixed Ratio</h3>
<p>Fixed number of responses के बाद reinforcement।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>हर पाँच assignments complete करने पर recognition।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">26.3 Variable Ratio</h3>
<p>Varying/unpredictable number of responses के बाद reinforcement।</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Behaviour highly persistent हो सकता है।</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">26.4 Fixed Interval</h3>
<p>Fixed time interval के बाद appropriate response reinforce होता है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>हर सप्ताह progress review।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">26.5 Variable Interval</h3>
<p>Unpredictable time intervals पर reinforcement।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Exam Formula</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Ratio = Number of Responses
Interval = Time</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Fixed = Predictable
Variable = Unpredictable</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">27. Shaping</h2>
<p>Complex behaviour को successive approximations के reinforcement द्वारा gradually develop करना।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>Research writing सिखाने में:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Correct research problem को reinforce करना</li><li>फिर objectives</li><li>फिर literature review</li><li>फिर complete proposal</li></ul>
<p class="mod-strong">Shaping = Reinforcement of Successive Approximations</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">28. Extinction</h2>
<p>यदि previously reinforced behaviour को reinforcement मिलना बन्द हो जाए, तो behaviour धीरे-धीरे कम हो सकता है।</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>Attention-seeking interruption को teacher reinforce करना बन्द कर देता है; समय के साथ behaviour कम हो सकता है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Exam Trap</h3>
<p>Extinction punishment नहीं है; इसमें reinforcement withdraw किया जाता है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">29. Programmed Instruction</h2>
<p>Skinner को Linear Programmed Instruction से associate किया जाता है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">प्रमुख Features</h3>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Content in small steps</li><li>Active learner response</li><li>Immediate feedback</li><li>Self-pacing</li><li>Continuous reinforcement</li><li>Minimum errors</li><li>Individualised progression</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Formula</h3>
<p class="mod-strong">Small Step → Active Response → Immediate Feedback → Reinforcement → Next Step</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Linear Programming</h3>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>सभी learners broadly same sequence follow करते हैं।</li><li>Skinner से associated है।</li><li>Small steps और correct response पर emphasis।</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Branching Programming</h3>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Response के अनुसार learner different path ले सकता है।</li><li>Norman Crowder से associated है।</li><li>Error diagnosis और remedial branch उपलब्ध हो सकती है।</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Exam Association</h3>
<p class="mod-tag">Skinner → Linear Programming</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Crowder → Branching Programming</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">30. Classroom Applications of Skinner</h2>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Immediate feedback</li><li>Specific praise</li><li>Token system</li><li>Drill and practice</li><li>Behaviour contracts</li><li>Programmed learning</li><li>Computer-assisted practice</li><li>Mastery of small steps</li><li>Reinforcing desired participation</li><li>Shaping complex skills</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Appropriate Praise</h3>
<p>Weak praise:</p>
<p>“Very good.”</p>
<p>Better reinforcement:</p>
<p>“आपने conclusion को relevant evidence से support किया है।”</p>
<p>Specific feedback learner को desired behaviour समझने में सहायता करता है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">31. Limitations of Skinner’s Approach</h2>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Observable behaviour पर अधिक emphasis</li><li>Internal thought और emotion की limited explanation</li><li>External rewards पर overdependence</li><li>Creativity और independent inquiry की उपेक्षा का risk</li><li>Complex learning को small responses तक reduce करने का खतरा</li><li>Reward हटने पर motivation कम हो सकती है</li></ul>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Balanced Approach</h3>
<p>Reinforcement basic habits और skills के लिए उपयोगी है, लेकिन higher-order learning में:</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Meaning</li><li>Inquiry</li><li>Reflection</li><li>Collaboration</li><li>Internal motivation</li></ul>
<p>भी आवश्यक हैं।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">32. Pavlov vs Skinner vs Bandura</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Recall Formula</h3>
<p class="mod-tag">Pavlov = Stimulus</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Skinner = Consequence</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Bandura = Model</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">33. Dewey vs Vygotsky vs Skinner</h2>
<h2 class="mod-h2">34. Important Exam Traps</h2>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Dewey → Pragmatism; Vygotsky → Social Constructivism; Skinner → Behaviourism।</li><li>Learning by Doing केवल activity नहीं; reflection आवश्यक है।</li><li>ZPD actual और potential development के बीच का area है।</li><li>Scaffolding temporary है।</li><li>MKO teacher, peer या expert हो सकता है।</li><li>Scaffolding term Wood, Bruner और Ross से associated है।</li><li>Negative reinforcement punishment नहीं है।</li><li>Reinforcement behaviour बढ़ाता है; punishment behaviour घटाता है।</li><li>Skinner Linear Programming; Crowder Branching Programming।</li><li>Pavlov stimulus association; Skinner consequences; Bandura modelling।</li><li>Dewey teacher को remove नहीं करते—teacher experiences organise करता है।</li><li>Skinner का approach observable behaviour पर अधिक focus करता है।</li></ul>
<h2 class="mod-h2">35. December 2026 Expected MCQs</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 1</h3>
<p>A teacher asks learners to investigate campus waste, analyse data and propose a solution. This approach is most closely associated with:</p>
<p>Teacher students से campus waste की जाँच, data analysis और solution बनाने को कहता है। यह किससे संबंधित है?</p>
<p>A. Classical conditioning
B. Learning by Doing
C. Rote learning
D. Programmed instruction</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-tag">B. Learning by Doing</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>Learners meaningful experience, inquiry और problem-solving में actively participate कर रहे हैं। यह Dewey की approach है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 2</h3>
<p>Which statement best represents Dewey’s concept of educational experience?</p>
<p>A. Every activity automatically produces learning.
B. Learning occurs only through memorisation.
C. Purposeful experience followed by reflection promotes growth.
D. Teacher control is the only basis of learning.</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-strong">C. Purposeful experience followed by reflection promotes growth.</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>Dewey के अनुसार activity को meaningful educational experience बनाने के लिए continuity, interaction और reflection आवश्यक हैं।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 3</h3>
<p>A learner cannot solve a problem independently but succeeds with guided hints. The task lies in the learner’s:</p>
<p>A. Conditioned-response zone
B. Zone of Proximal Development
C. Formal-operational stage only
D. Reinforcement schedule</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-tag">B. Zone of Proximal Development</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>ZPD उस task को दर्शाता है जिसे learner independent रूप से नहीं, लेकिन guidance के साथ कर सकता है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 4</h3>
<p>Which of the following is the best example of scaffolding?</p>
<p>A. Giving the complete answer every time
B. Providing temporary hints and gradually withdrawing them
C. Punishing every incorrect response
D. Requiring rote repetition without feedback</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-strong">B. Providing temporary hints and gradually withdrawing them</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>Scaffolding temporary support है, permanent dependence नहीं।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 5</h3>
<p>In Vygotsky’s theory, a More Knowledgeable Other can be:</p>
<p>A. Only a formal teacher
B. Only a parent
C. A teacher, skilled peer or expert
D. Only a computer</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-tag">C. A teacher, skilled peer or expert</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>MKO कोई भी person या support source हो सकता है जिसके पास specific task में greater competence हो।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 6</h3>
<p>A student completes work on time, after which the teacher removes an additional remedial task. This is:</p>
<p>A. Positive punishment
B. Negative punishment
C. Positive reinforcement
D. Negative reinforcement</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-tag">D. Negative Reinforcement</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>Unpleasant condition हटाई गई और desired behaviour बढ़ाने का उद्देश्य है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 7</h3>
<p>Which statement about reinforcement is correct?</p>
<p>A. Reinforcement always decreases behaviour.
B. Negative reinforcement is identical to punishment.
C. Reinforcement aims to increase behaviour.
D. Positive reinforcement means adding punishment.</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-strong">C. Reinforcement aims to increase behaviour.</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>Positive और negative दोनों reinforcement behaviour बढ़ाते हैं; difference stimulus add या remove करने का है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 8</h3>
<p>Which pair is correctly matched?</p>
<p>A. Dewey—Operant Conditioning
B. Vygotsky—ZPD
C. Skinner—Insight Learning
D. Köhler—Programmed Instruction</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-tag">B. Vygotsky—ZPD</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>Dewey Learning by Doing, Skinner Operant Conditioning और Köhler Insight Learning से संबंधित हैं।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 9</h3>
<p>The correct sequence in Skinner’s programmed instruction is:</p>
<p>A. Large content → delayed response → final feedback
B. Small step → active response → immediate feedback → reinforcement
C. Observation → imitation → delayed punishment
D. Problem → hypothesis → experiment → reflection</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-strong">B. Small step → active response → immediate feedback → reinforcement</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>यह Linear Programmed Instruction की central process है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 10: Assertion–Reason</h3>
<p>Assertion: Negative reinforcement is not punishment.
Reason: Negative reinforcement increases behaviour by removing an unpleasant condition.</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Options</p>
<p>A. Both Assertion and Reason are true, and Reason correctly explains Assertion.
B. Both are true, but Reason does not explain Assertion.
C. Assertion is true, but Reason is false.
D. Assertion is false, but Reason is true.</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-strong">A. Both are true, and Reason correctly explains Assertion.</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 11</h3>
<p>Which association is incorrect?</p>
<p>A. Skinner—Linear Programming
B. Crowder—Branching Programming
C. Vygotsky—Social Constructivism
D. Dewey—Rote Learning</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-tag">D. Dewey—Rote Learning</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<p>Dewey activity, experience, inquiry और reflective learning से associated हैं।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 12</h3>
<p>Which classroom situation best integrates Dewey, Vygotsky and Skinner?</p>
<p>A. Learners silently memorise notes without feedback.
B. Learners solve a real problem collaboratively, receive guided support and obtain immediate constructive feedback.
C. Teacher gives the final answer and prevents discussion.
D. Learners are punished for proposing alternative solutions.</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer</p>
<p class="mod-strong">B. Learners solve a real problem collaboratively, receive guided support and obtain immediate constructive feedback.</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Explanation</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Real problem and activity → Dewey</li><li>Collaborative guidance → Vygotsky</li><li>Immediate constructive reinforcement → Skinner</li></ul>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="mod-table"><tr><th>Basis</th><th>Piaget</th><th>Vygotsky</th></tr><tr><td>Theory</td><td>Cognitive Constructivism</td><td>Social Constructivism</td></tr><tr><td>Main focus</td><td>Individual cognitive development</td><td>Social-cultural interaction</td></tr><tr><td>Development</td><td>Stages पर emphasis</td><td>Social guidance पर emphasis</td></tr><tr><td>Language</td><td>Cognitive development follows/affects language</td><td>Language cognition को shape करती है</td></tr><tr><td>Teacher role</td><td>Discovery environment</td><td>Guided participation/scaffolding</td></tr><tr><td>Peer/Adult role</td><td>Peer interaction useful</td><td>MKO central role</td></tr><tr><td>Key concept</td><td>Assimilation–Accommodation</td><td>ZPD–Scaffolding</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="mod-table"><tr><th>Concept</th><th>What happens?</th><th>Effect on behaviour</th></tr><tr><td>Positive Reinforcement</td><td>Pleasant stimulus added</td><td>Behaviour increases</td></tr><tr><td>Negative Reinforcement</td><td>Unpleasant stimulus removed</td><td>Behaviour increases</td></tr><tr><td>Positive Punishment</td><td>Unpleasant consequence added</td><td>Behaviour decreases</td></tr><tr><td>Negative Punishment</td><td>Pleasant privilege removed</td><td>Behaviour decreases</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="mod-table"><tr><th>Basis</th><th>Pavlov</th><th>Skinner</th><th>Bandura</th></tr><tr><td>Theory</td><td>Classical Conditioning</td><td>Operant Conditioning</td><td>Observational Learning</td></tr><tr><td>Learning basis</td><td>Stimulus association</td><td>Consequences</td><td>Observation/model</td></tr><tr><td>Behaviour</td><td>More respondent/involuntary</td><td>Operant/voluntary</td><td>Observed and reproduced</td></tr><tr><td>Key concept</td><td>CS–CR association</td><td>Reinforcement</td><td>Modelling</td></tr><tr><td>Example</td><td>Classroom से anxiety</td><td>Praise increases participation</td><td>Learner copies demonstration</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="mod-table"><tr><th>Basis</th><th>Dewey</th><th>Vygotsky</th><th>Skinner</th></tr><tr><td>Broad orientation</td><td>Pragmatism</td><td>Social Constructivism</td><td>Behaviourism</td></tr><tr><td>Learning source</td><td>Experience and activity</td><td>Social-cultural interaction</td><td>Behaviour consequences</td></tr><tr><td>Key concept</td><td>Learning by Doing</td><td>ZPD and scaffolding</td><td>Reinforcement</td></tr><tr><td>Learner role</td><td>Active investigator</td><td>Social participant</td><td>Active responder</td></tr><tr><td>Teacher role</td><td>Experience designer</td><td>Guide/scaffold provider</td><td>Behaviour organiser</td></tr><tr><td>Classroom method</td><td>Project/problem-solving</td><td>Collaboration/guided learning</td><td>Practice and reinforcement</td></tr><tr><td>Motivation</td><td>Meaningful experience</td><td>Participation and support</td><td>Reinforcement</td></tr><tr><td>Main outcome</td><td>Reflective problem-solving</td><td>Independent competence</td><td>Behaviour acquisition</td></tr><tr><td>Assessment focus</td><td>Application and reflection</td><td>Assisted-to-independent growth</td><td>Observable performance</td></tr></table></div>
    </article>
